 "findings": [
  {
   "finding": "Live union-scope state at protocol 1e6cdf04d7a2: 10 binding rows = 5 accept / 5 dissent; 4 of the dissents target N0 (node reviews that cite the protocol hash), 2 target the document. The tool reports reviewed=true, contest=true.",
   "id": "W020-PRS-01",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "finding": "Scope conflation is real: the union target scope (path, G-NUM-protocol, N0) counts an N0-node revise as a protocol-document dissent. The three N0-targeted dissents (067-provledger 00:51:49, 042-stoprule 00:52:59, 081-pinsplit 00:58:18) are node verdicts, not document verdicts; under document scope they are excluded (rules R2/R3).",
   "id": "W020-PRS-02",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "finding": "No supersession: the live accepted_reviews list keeps 081-c8 (00:21:40) and 081-adj2 (00:42:05) while dissenting_reviews keeps 081-f1adj (00:29:19), although 081-adj2 is later than 081-f1adj and retracts it in its own text (DISPOSITION F1_AND_F1PRIME_DISCHARGED_BY_SUPERSESSION). R3/R4 remove 081-f1adj and keep 081-adj2 as 081's operative document verdict.",
   "id": "W020-PRS-03",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "finding": "Supersession and scope alone do NOT clear the live contest. R3 (document scope + latest per reviewer) still reports contest=true with exactly one standing dissent: worker-067 w067-review-gnum-protocol-r3 (revise 4.0, 00:22:56, path#hash target, F1 major: section 3.4 text must be scoped in rev 4). Worker-067 published no later document verdict, so the correct controller statement is 'one standing document revise', not 'no contest'.",
   "id": "W020-PRS-04",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "finding": "Correction to B-N0-R2-2's chronology: 081's adj2 accept (00:42:05) supersedes only its own f1adj revise (00:29:19). 081's later binding verdict is the pinsplit revise (00:58:18, N0 target), which is later than adj2 and is what withdraws 081's c8 accept under union scope. A (reviewer,target)-supersession rule (R4) therefore leaves 081 as accept-on-document + revise-on-N0 simultaneously; only document scope + per-reviewer supersession (R3) yields a single coherent 081 document position (accept).",
   "id": "W020-PRS-05",
   "severity": "advisory"
  },
  {
   "finding": "Candidate semantics for controller disposition (not adopted here): (a) score the protocol on document-targeted verdicts (path or G-NUM-protocol) and keep N0-targeted verdicts for node N0; (b) supersede per (reviewer, scope) by created_at with dissent winning exact ties; (c) keep the union scope only for the 'is there any independent accept' predicate, not for contest. Live effect of that candidate (R3): reviewed=true, contest=true with the single standing dissent 067-r3; the remaining blocker is substantive (067 F1 vs 081-adj2/flash-12 C3 discharge), not mechanical.",
   "id": "W020-PRS-06",
   "severity": "advisory"
  },
  {
   "finding": "Controls: 16/16 truth-table cases matched declared expectations; live-source drift at audit time: 1 file(s). Advisory rows at superseded hashes: 4 (reported separately, do not bind).",
   "id": "W020-PRS-07",
   "severity": "info"
  }
 ],
